= Governance — Technical =

Governance can be analyzed as an institutional system with actors, decision rights, information flows, rule-making procedures, monitoring, enforcement, appeal/conflict-resolution mechanisms, and amendment processes. Formal rules and de facto power can diverge, so institutional analysis must examine both.

== Modeling cautions ==
* governance ≠ government
* governance ≠ voting only
* formal rules ≠ actual institutional behavior

== References ==
* World Bank, ''World Development Report 2017: Governance and the Law''.
* World Bank, Worldwide Governance Indicators documentation, for one institutional definition and measurement framework.
* Elinor Ostrom, ''Understanding Institutional Diversity'' (2005).
